# Nimble 3rd Party Creator License v2.0 — Compliance Implementation Plan

Source license: [nimbleRPG.com/pages/creators](https://nimblerpg.com/pages/creators), updated December 9, 2025.
This plan tracks what Nimble RPG App must do to comply with each clause of the license, what's already in place, and what's still missing.

## 1. Required attribution notice

**Requirement:** Product must include: *"[Product Name] is an independent product published under the Nimble 3rd Party Creator License. Nimble © Nimble Co."*

**Current state:** [about.md](../about.md) and [About.tsx](../client/Settings/components/About.tsx) both link to the license and credit content sources, but neither uses the required sentence — no "is an independent product" disclaimer and no "Nimble © Nimble Co." line.

**Action items:**

- [x] Rewrote the attribution paragraph in [About.tsx](../client/Settings/components/About.tsx#L44-L69) to include the verbatim required sentence: "Nimble RPG App is an independent product published under the Nimble 3rd Party Creator License. Nimble © Nimble Co."
- [x] Applied the same wording to [about.md](../about.md)
- [x] Updated the same attribution block in [landing.html](../html/landing.html#L128-L156)
- [x] Confirmed none of these spots imply official endorsement — wording is descriptive ("independent product," "content provided under terms of") not "official"/"endorsed"

## 2. "Free to use" notice for online apps/VTTs

**Requirement:** Since this is a free online tool using published Nimble text, it must prominently display (banner, sidebar, welcome message, etc.): *"This app is free to use for anyone who already owns the content, is trying the system out, or cannot afford to buy it right now. If you enjoy Nimble and are able, please support the game by purchasing the official content at nimbleRPG.com."*

**Current state:** Not found anywhere in the codebase — no match for this notice in [landing.html](../html/landing.html), [tracker.html](../html/tracker.html), or any component. This is the largest compliance gap.

**Action items:**

- [x] Added the required notice text to:
  - [x] [About.tsx](../client/Settings/components/About.tsx) (Settings > About tab, next to attribution)
  - [x] [landing.html](../html/landing.html) (footer, next to attribution — marketing/welcome page shown to anonymous visitors)
  - [x] [about.md](../about.md)
- [x] Notice text used verbatim in all three locations
- [ ] Optional: consider surfacing it in the [Tutorial](../client/Tutorial/Tutorial.tsx)/[TutorialSteps.ts](../client/Tutorial/TutorialSteps.ts) welcome flow too — not done, footer/About placement was judged sufficient for "prominently displayed"

## 3. "Completely free to use" — audit monetization against Nimble content

**Requirement:** The free-online-tool exemption only applies if the tool is "completely free to use (optional donations to defray development/hosting costs permitted)." Nimble content specifically must not be paywalled.

**Current state:** The app has a Patreon-gated "Epic Initiative" tier (see [EpicInitiativeSettings.tsx](../client/Settings/components/EpicInitiativeSettings.tsx)). On inspection, gated features are cosmetic/account features — Account Sync, Player View styling/CSS, portraits, custom Player View URL, tag suggestions, banner removal, D&D Beyond importer — not Nimble rules text, stat blocks, or bestiary content. This looks consistent with "optional donations," but hasn't been exhaustively verified.

**Action items:**

- [x] Audited [Libraries.ts](../client/Library/Libraries.ts): stat block/spell preloading and library sync run unconditionally on load — no `HasEpicInitiative`/`HasAccountSync`/`HasMythic` (or `IsLoggedIn`) checks anywhere in `client/Library/`. Login only adds account-synced custom data on top of the free local library; it doesn't gate any Nimble content.
- [x] Free tier can fully build encounters and run combat with official Nimble content — no Nimble-text feature is gated behind a paid tier
- [ ] Document the "donations only, no content paywalls" rule in [CONTRIBUTING.md](../CONTRIBUTING.md) so future paid-tier features don't accidentally gate Nimble content

## 4. Art and logo restrictions

**Requirement:** May not use Nimble's own art or logo. May use the Nimble compatibility logo instead (from nimbleRPG.com/creators).

**Current state:** In-progress rebranding is visible in git status — old `boot-*`/`shield-*` assets are being replaced with `book-*` icons and `logo-patreon-nimble-rpg-app.svg`. The app's live landing page and manifest still reference leftover *Improved Initiative* branding ([manifest.json](../public/manifest.json), [landing.html](../html/landing.html#L32-L67): `logo-improved-initiative.svg`, `improved-initiative-transparent-darkgreen.png`), which isn't Nimble art but is stale/confusing branding from the fork.

**Action items:**

- [x] Confirmed `beige-paper.png`, `dark-texture.png`, and `paper-bg.jpg` under [public/img/](../public/img/) are original/licensed-generic textures, not sourced from official Nimble books/art
- [x] Replaced `logo-improved-initiative.svg` / `improved-initiative-transparent-darkgreen.png` references in [landing.html](../html/landing.html) (header logo, og:image, twitter:image, image_src) and [tracker.html](../html/tracker.html) (og:image) with `book-transparent-white.png` / `book-white-on-black-512.png`. [manifest.json](../public/manifest.json) already used the book icons.
- [ ] No "Nimble compatibility logo" asset from nimbleRPG.com/creators exists in the repo yet — needs to be downloaded from that page and added manually if you want to display it explicitly (not something I can fetch/verify licensing on myself)
- [ ] Stray `AD` (added-then-deleted) image files still show in `git status` (`ShieldLogo.png`, `Gemini_Generated_Image_...jfif`, `shield-*.png`) — stage the deletions with `git add` once you're done with the branding pass, or restore them if they were deleted by accident

## 5. Copying/restating large portions of text

**Requirement:** Copying, restating, or summarizing large portions of Nimble text with little added content doesn't qualify as an "original product."

**Current state:** Needs review — this is a content question (how much raw rules/monster text is reproduced vs. transformed into app functionality) rather than a code change.

**Action items:**

- [ ] Review the stat block / reference content shipped in the library data for verbatim reproduction of large rules sections without added tooling value (the app's combat-tracking functionality itself likely satisfies "added content," but worth a deliberate check)

## 6. Legal terms (indemnification, termination, governing law)

**Requirement:** No direct implementation action — these clauses govern the relationship between the creator (Eddy Wong) and Nimble Co., not end users. Nimble Co. disclaims liability for the product; the creator indemnifies Nimble Co.; the license can be terminated on violation.

**Current state:** [PRIVACY.md](../PRIVACY.md) already has a "TERMS OF SERVICE" section disclaiming warranty to end users, which is a separate concern from this clause.

**Action items:**

- [ ] None required for app implementation. Keep in mind: if any required item above (attribution, free-to-use notice, content paywalling) goes unaddressed, that's the kind of violation that could trigger termination — treat items 1–4 as the actual compliance work.

